cpp-coding-guide: Adding to this thread. The two selector locals at `src/tron/kernels/amx_attn.cpp:174-175` are `constexpr`, so the guide's naming rule applies to them as well: `pair_sel` and `quad_sel` become `PAIR_SEL` and `QUAD_SEL` (uppercase with underscores). The only other function-local constexpr in this file, `P_ROW_BYTES` at `:294`, already follows that rule. Together with the named masks proposed above:

```cpp
  constexpr int PAIR_SEL = (lane & STAGE3_LANE_BIT_1) ? LANES_ODD_0XDD : LANES_EVEN_0X88;
  constexpr int QUAD_SEL = (lane & STAGE4_LANE_BIT_2) ? LANES_ODD_0XDD : LANES_EVEN_0X88;
```

The uses at `:178`, `:179` and `:181` follow.
